# Plan M7, step 4 (the author, 2026-11-10; the book, forms-declare-or-call): a structural form declares or calls and writes
# no known place.  In the body of a named Structure too: `y: 7` after `int: y 3` is a statement of the
# body's procedure, a write of the known place y by a form with a colon -- refused where the procedure is lowered.  Before, the
# form was an assignment and counted as a second root head of y (slice 276, occurrence_bare_refused).
D:
    int: y 3
    y: 7
end: D
send: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
